BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Naza | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261026T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261026T203000
UID:d602b2bdb61c3895e1c0fb6e1513d3c5@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Oscar-winning documentarians Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor spe
 nt three years investigating the technological systems inherent to modern 
 warfare\, uncovering their inner workings from the people who designed the
 m. Through interviews with two dozen intelligence officers and soldiers\, 
 the film unfolds how civilian causalities are increasing as warfare become
 s increasingly technologized and AI-assisted. While the revelations uncove
 red during the film were published in real-time by The Guardian and other 
 outlets over the last three years\, the film's power lies in the unvarnish
 ed testimony of its participants\, letting their own words contextualize t
 heir decisions. Winner of the Special Jury Prize at the 83rd Venice Intern
 ational Film Festival. [80 min\; documentary\; Hebrew with English subtitl
 es]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/naza-additional-films-and-guest
 s/60004/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
