BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Concert Band &#8211\; Jason H. Nam\, conductor &#8211\; “Of Eart
 h and Sky\,” Featuring graduate student conductor Nick Hinman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T213000
UID:4d78bc13eedc3f7f1315cb274bb86299@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world via L
 IVE@jacobs!\nRepertoire\nSteven Bryant: In This Broad Earth (2015)\nJoni G
 reene: Splitting Light (2026\, consortium premiere)\nGala Flagello: Love a
 nd Nature (2024)\nAaron Perrine: Pale Blue on Deep (2011)\nDana Wilson: Co
 lorado Peaks (2005)\nJohn Mackey: Aurora Awakes (2009)\nAbout the Conducto
 r\nJason H. Nam is associate professor of music in bands at the Indiana Un
 iversity Jacobs School of Music\, where he conducts bands and teaches unde
 rgraduate and graduate courses in instrumental conducting\, administration
  of school bands\, and wind literature. Nam earned a Doctor of Music in Wi
 nd Conducting degree from the Jacobs School\, where he studied with Stephe
 n W. Pratt. He earned an M.M. in Conducting and a B.M. in Music Education 
 from the University of Redlands\, where he studied with Eddie R. Smith. Na
 m served as a lecturer in the Department of Music at California State Univ
 ersity\, San Bernardino\, and as director of bands at La Colina Junior Hig
 h School and San Marcos High School in Santa Barbara\, California. More re
 cently\, he has served as a faculty member\, ensemble conductor\, and dire
 ctor of the IU Summer Music Clinic. Nam keeps a busy schedule as conductor
 \, adjudicator\, and clinician across North America. He was named a nation
 al finalist for The American Prize in Conducting (Band/Wind Ensemble divis
 ion) in 2017 amd 2023. His IU Concert Band was invited to perform at the 2
 020 College Band Directors National Association North Central Conference i
 n Chicago\, Illinois. Nam served as resident music director of the Bloomin
 gton-based Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble from 2016 to 2021\, performing w
 idely throughout Indiana and as an invited ensemble at the Ohio Music Educ
 ators Professional Development Conference in 2020. He has been published i
 n the Journal of the National Band Association and the American Bandmaster
 s Association’s Journal of Band Research. His research interests include
  the music of William Bolcom\, the wind chamber music of Igor Stravinsky\,
  the historical development of the wind band repertoire in the twentieth c
 entury\, and effective rehearsal methodologies for conductors. Nam current
 ly serves on the national selection committee for the National Band Associ
 ation/William D. Revelli Memorial Band Composition Contest and holds profe
 ssional memberships in the College Band Directors National Association\, N
 ational Band Association\, Conductors Guild\, Indiana Music Education Asso
 ciation\, and Pi Kappa Lambda music honor society.
GEO:39.1665575;-86.51751229999999
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 101 N Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47406
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/concert-band-8211-jason-h-nam-c
 onductor-8211-of-earth-and-sky-featuring-graduate-student-conductor-nick-h
 inman/59658/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everybody to Kenmure Street | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T204500
UID:78a2441cf389c42240c445d1937bd3a4@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The first day of Eid in Glasgow started as any other. But soon
 \, neighbors heard through community message networks that two local men w
 ere snatched up for deportation\, and suddenly hundreds of people left the
 ir breakfast tables\, work Zoom calls\, and daily lives to rush down to Ke
 nmure Street to save them by putting their bodies on the line. Though most
 ly strangers\, and with almost no planning\, this extremely diverse group 
 organized themselves\, taking on essential roles to allow the collective t
 o protect their own from government forces targeting their least protected
  neighbors. An inspiring and profoundly moving portrait of what we all are
  capable of in the face of injustice\, Everybody to Kenmure Street reminds
  us of the power that is always inherent in the people. Winner\, World Cin
 ema Documentary Special Jury Award for Civil Resistance\, Sundance Film Fe
 stival 2026. [95 min\; documentary\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/everybody-to-kenmure-street-art
 house-now/59866/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
