  capital\, employers\, talent\, and partners in the same room\, on purpose
 . It's free and open to the public\, October 28–30\, across five venues 
 in Bloomington. Opening night at the Buskirk-Chumley Theater features a ke
 ynote from Mike Clem\, CEO of Sweetwater. The following days bring session
 s across the city\, the IN AI Roadshow\, a lunch keynote from IU Kelley's 
 Tatiana Kolovou\, and the IU Innovates Startup Showcase — all leading in
 to IU Homecoming weekend. Whether you're building a company\, backing one
 \, hiring\, or finding a reason to build your career here\, there's a plac
 e for you in the room. Register free.
