BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tarot Readings with Scott Kellogg on Saturdays at oak.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261219T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261219T160000
UID:13bfe0096d103fe74a045e740dc76a7a@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Beginning February 14\, Oak welcomes Scott Kellogg as our resi
 dent tarot reader. With over twenty years of experience as a tarot practit
 ioner\, teacher\, and community builder\, Scott offers readings that are i
 ntuitive\, thoughtful\, and deeply attuned to the person across the table.
 \nHis work gently explores your inner landscape\, your emotions\, desires
 \, and the unseen patterns shaping your life. These sessions are less abou
 t prediction and more about remembrance\, helping you reconnect with your 
 inner knowing and the quiet wisdom you already carry.\nScott holds space w
 ith care\, curiosity\, and respect\, creating a grounded and welcoming exp
 erience for women and femme centered seekers at every stage of life. A rea
 ding with Scott invites clarity\, reassurance\, and a sense of being truly
  seen.
GEO:39.167879;-86.53442559999999
LOCATION:oak.\, 116 W 6th Street\, Suite 101\, Bloomington\, IN 47401
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/tarot-readings-with-scott-kello
 gg-on-saturdays-at-oak/57842/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Coll
 ection
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261220
UID:eea2bc03de191e7b81a05e90a2c3465d@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Spanning more than 150 years\, The Photographic Reflex celebra
 tes a transformative gift to the Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana Univers
 ity: more than one hundred works by eighty artists\, generously donated by
  Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. This exhibition features photographs dat
 ing from 1856 to 2017 and highlights the medium’s extraordinary range\, 
 both as a tool for documentation and as a vehicle for artistic exploration
 .\nFrom Alfred Stieglitz’s delicate studies of grass to Richard Misrach
 ’s vast images of the cosmos\, photographers have long found inspiration
  in the natural world. The built environment has also served as a compelli
 ng subject\, and the exhibition includes Berenice Abbott’s striking view
 s of 1920s New York City as well as Edward Burtynsky’s sweeping industri
 al landscapes.\nPhotography has played a central role in witnessing confli
 ct\, from Timothy H. O’Sullivan’s Civil War battlefield to iconic imag
 es from World War II\, Vietnam\, and beyond. While often associated with s
 traightforward depictions of reality\, photography also allows artists to 
 experiment with light\, exposure\, and process to construct imaginative sc
 enes and images beyond human sight.\nThe Photographic Reflex: The Lee Mark
 s and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection reveals photography’s power to refle
 ct and shape our perception of the world around us across time\, space\, a
 nd vision.\nLead support for this exhibition has been generously provided 
 by the Martha and David Moore Prints\, Drawings and Photographs Endowment
 \; Peter and Pamela DePrez\; Anne Marks Morgan\; Gregory Morse\; Efroymson
  Family Fund\; Anne N. DePrez\; John J. Medveckis\; and Friends of Lee Mar
 ks and John DePrez Jr.\nAdditional support provided by John M. (Jack) Reyn
 olds\, Jeffrey A. Wolin\, Sandi Clark\, and Katherine Campbell and Robert 
 J. Boeglin Jr.\, M.D.
GEO:39.1688819;-86.5198163
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University\, 1133 E. 7th Street
 \, Fine Arts Plaza\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-photographic-reflex-the-lee
 -marks-and-john-c-deprez-jr-collection/60101/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Krampus Bizaar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261220T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261220T180000
UID:22e6754978c8603fd574f16d8f3bf449@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Can you hear the bells? Can you hear the hooves clacking throu
 gh the streets? It's that time again - KRAMPUS COMES TO BLOOMINGTON. Join 
 us for the Krampus Bizaar\, where you can find whimsical vendors\, spooky 
 items\, naughty elves\, angels spreading cheer and much more. We will have
  35+ vendors setup at the pavilion in Switchyard Park along with food vend
 ors and all manner of roaming critters.\nThis is a free-to-attend\, kid-fr
 iendly event to help support local makers and keep the spirit of Krampus a
 live. This time of year we are thinking about gifts and what we want to ta
 ke into the next year\, but it's also an opportunity to get in tune with o
 ur ancestors and those who have passed on. Come down for an oracle\, rune
 \, or tarot reading\, get some reiki healing and prepare yourself to tuck 
 in for those long winter nights.
GEO:39.1476298;-86.5384061
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S. Rogers Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47403
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/krampus-bizaar/59600/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
